  "hypothesis": "A strict cohort timestamp applied to every asset ledger, combined with immutable source-run episode attribution, can produce causally coherent live-prefix deltas that distinguish resolved venue economics from repeated or newly matured counterfactual opportunity paths without creating execution authority.",
  "decision": "Retain the running v25 strategy unchanged. The corrected 27.53-minute delta resolves one exact compatible SOL HT-Breakout lifecycle at +$1.582877 net after fees and funding, but only one of 33 newly independent exact episode paths clears the fixed 13 bps close hurdle and none adds robust-MFE support. Cumulative independent means remain negative at every 5/15/30/60-minute horizon. The first destination audit exposed and the implementation now prevents a cross-ledger snapshot race in which a post-cutoff asset close could be combined with an earlier cohort state. This materially improves evidence validity but does not authorize a route, blocker, sizing, risk, exit-policy, restart, drain, order, close, resize, or promotion change.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "falsifier": "The monitoring method is falsified by admitting an asset row observed after the cohort cutoff, allowing a resolved episode path to disappear or change identity, fabricating comparability when an earlier prefix lacks attribution, counting unchanged attribution rows as changed, accepting mismatched run/profile identity, changing immutable evidence, introducing execution authority, or mutating live runtime state. The economic decision is updated by materially more independent venue-resolved lifecycles and episode paths with consistent after-fee, after-funding, after-friction outcomes and non-outlier robustness.",
